IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `sgta-nouns`

-- Telecommunications Act 1999 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation (TA1999.txt).
-- PART 7 INTERNATIONAL OBLIGATIONS AND NATIONAL INTERESTS: ss 72 to 77.
-- Seat: the public telecommunication licensee or telecommunication licensee (the person these sections bind), and the person whose
-- messages or equipment a direction under s 77 may reach.

§ `ss 72 to 76: international dealings and services to Government`

-- src:5431 | 72. For the purposes of the conduct of any international
-- src:5432 | telecommunication service by a public telecommunication licensee,
-- src:5433 | and subject to this Act, the licensee may enter into direct
-- src:5434 | communication, arrangement and agreement with the lawfully
-- src:5435 | constituted telecommunication authority of any country or with any
-- src:5436 | duly authorised international agency or organisation concerned with
-- src:5437 | telecommunication matters —
-- src:5439 | (a) for the purpose of providing facilities, fixing rates,
-- src:5440 | arranging terms of payment or accounting;
-- src:5442 | (b) for operational, engineering or administrative purposes; or
-- src:5444 | (c) for any other purpose necessary for the proper fulfilment of
-- src:5445 | its functions.
@ref s 72 (src:5431-5445)
GIVEN `the dealing is for the conduct of an international telecommunication service by a public telecommunication licensee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the counterparty is the lawfully constituted telecommunication authority of a country or a duly authorised international agency or organisation concerned with telecommunication matters` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the purpose is providing facilities, fixing rates, arranging terms of payment or accounting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the purpose is operational, engineering or administrative` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the purpose is another purpose necessary for the proper fulfilment of the licensee's functions` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 72: the licensee may enter into direct communication, arrangement and agreement with the counterparty` MEANS
        `the dealing is for the conduct of an international telecommunication service by a public telecommunication licensee`
    AND `the counterparty is the lawfully constituted telecommunication authority of a country or a duly authorised international agency or organisation concerned with telecommunication matters`
    AND (   `the purpose is providing facilities, fixing rates, arranging terms of payment or accounting`
         OR `the purpose is operational, engineering or administrative`
         OR `the purpose is another purpose necessary for the proper fulfilment of the licensee's functions`)

-- src:5450 | 73.—(1) Nothing in section 72 is deemed to abrogate the right of
-- src:5451 | the Government at any time to determine its relations with any
-- src:5452 | country or with any international agency or organisation.
-- src:5454 | (2) A public telecommunication licensee must so discharge its
-- src:5455 | responsibilities and conduct its business as to comply with and fulfil
-- src:5456 | all international agreements, conventions or undertakings relating to
-- src:5457 | telecommunication to which Singapore is a party.
@ref s 73 (src:5450-5457)
GIVEN `the Government determines its relations with a country or an international agency or organisation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 73(1): section 72 abrogates the Government's right to determine its relations` MEANS
    FALSE

GIVEN `the licensee complies with and fulfils all international agreements, conventions or undertakings relating to telecommunication to which Singapore is a party` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 73(2): the public telecommunication licensee has discharged its responsibilities as the subsection requires` MEANS
    `the licensee complies with and fulfils all international agreements, conventions or undertakings relating to telecommunication to which Singapore is a party`

-- src:5463 | 74. A public telecommunication licensee is fully responsible for
-- src:5464 | meeting all financial obligations arising from the operation of any
-- src:5465 | international telecommunication service and must settle accounts
-- src:5466 | with other telecommunication authorities.
@ref s 74 (src:5463-5466)
GIVEN `the obligation arises from the operation of an international telecommunication service` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 74: the public telecommunication licensee is fully responsible for meeting the financial obligation and must settle accounts with other telecommunication authorities` MEANS
    `the obligation arises from the operation of an international telecommunication service`

-- src:5475 | 75. Where the Government considers it necessary that any
-- src:5476 | telecommunication service of an exceptional nature should be
-- src:5477 | provided, and where a public telecommunication licensee considers
-- src:5478 | it uneconomic to provide the service without contribution from the
-- src:5479 | Government, the Government may make such contribution towards
-- src:5480 | the capital outlay necessary to provide any such service as may be
-- src:5481 | estimated by the licensee and agreed to by the Government.
@ref s 75 (src:5475-5481)
GIVEN `the Government considers it necessary that a telecommunication service of an exceptional nature be provided` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the public telecommunication licensee considers it uneconomic to provide the service without a contribution from the Government` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 75: the Government may contribute towards the capital outlay, as estimated by the licensee and agreed to by the Government` MEANS
    `the Government considers it necessary that a telecommunication service of an exceptional nature be provided` AND `the public telecommunication licensee considers it uneconomic to provide the service without a contribution from the Government`

-- src:5487 | 76.—(1) The Minister may direct a public telecommunication
-- src:5488 | licensee to undertake and provide such telecommunication services
-- src:5489 | and facilities as may be necessary for aeronautical, maritime,
-- src:5490 | meteorological, governmental, defence or other purposes.
-- src:5492 | (2) Upon being so directed by the Minister, the public
-- src:5493 | telecommunication licensee must provide the telecommunication
-- src:5494 | services or facilities mentioned in subsection (1), and is entitled to
-- src:5495 | fair and proper payment for that.
@ref s 76 (src:5487-5495)
GIVEN `the service or facility is necessary for aeronautical, maritime, meteorological, governmental, defence or other purposes` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 76(1): the Minister may direct the public telecommunication licensee to undertake and provide the service or facility` MEANS
    `the service or facility is necessary for aeronautical, maritime, meteorological, governmental, defence or other purposes`

GIVEN `the Minister has so directed the public telecommunication licensee` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 76(2): the licensee must provide the service or facility and is entitled to fair and proper payment` MEANS
    `the Minister has so directed the public telecommunication licensee`

§ `s 77 Directions by Minister`

-- src:5501 | 77.—(1) The Minister may, after consultation with the Authority or
-- src:5502 | any telecommunication licensee, give to the Authority or licensee (as
-- src:5503 | the case may be) such directions as the Minister thinks fit as to the
-- src:5504 | exercise by the Authority or that licensee of its functions under this
-- src:5505 | Act.
@ref s 77(1) (src:5501-5505)
GIVEN `the Minister consulted the Authority or the telecommunication licensee` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 77(1): the Minister may give the Authority or licensee the direction as to the exercise of its functions under the Act` MEANS
    `the Minister consulted the Authority or the telecommunication licensee`

-- src:5509 | (2) Without affecting subsection (1), if it appears to the Minister to
-- src:5510 | be requisite or expedient to do so —
-- src:5512 | (a) on the occurrence of any public emergency, in the public
-- src:5513 | interest or in the interests of public security, national
-- src:5514 | defence, or relations with the government of another
-- src:5515 | country; or
-- src:5517 | Informal Consolidation – version in force from 2/10/2026
-- src:5518 | 2020 Ed. Telecommunications Act 1999 112
-- src:5520 | (b) in order —
-- src:5522 | (i) to discharge or facilitate the discharge of an
-- src:5523 | obligation binding on the Government by virtue of
-- src:5524 | its being a member of an international organisation
-- src:5525 | or a party to an international agreement;
-- src:5527 | (ii) to attain or facilitate the attainment of any other
-- src:5528 | object the attainment of which is in the opinion of the
-- src:5529 | Minister requisite or expedient in view of the
-- src:5530 | Government being a member of an international
-- src:5531 | organisation or a party to an international agreement;
-- src:5532 | or
-- src:5534 | (iii) to enable the Government to become a member of an
-- src:5535 | international organisation or a party to an
-- src:5536 | international agreement,
-- src:5538 | the Minister may, after consultation with the Authority or any
-- src:5539 | telecommunication licensee, give such directions to the Authority or
-- src:5540 | that licensee as are necessary in the circumstances of the case.
@ref s 77(2) (src:5509-5540)
GIVEN `it appears to the Minister requisite or expedient, on the occurrence of a public emergency, in the public interest, or in the interests of public security, national defence or relations with the government of another country` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it appears to the Minister requisite or expedient in order to discharge or facilitate the discharge of an obligation binding on the Government as a member of an international organisation or a party to an international agreement, to attain any other object requisite or expedient in view of that membership, or to enable the Government to become a member or party` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister consulted the Authority or the telecommunication licensee` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 77(2): the Minister may give such directions as are necessary in the circumstances of the case` MEANS
    (`it appears to the Minister requisite or expedient, on the occurrence of a public emergency, in the public interest, or in the interests of public security, national defence or relations with the government of another country` OR `it appears to the Minister requisite or expedient in order to discharge or facilitate the discharge of an obligation binding on the Government as a member of an international organisation or a party to an international agreement, to attain any other object requisite or expedient in view of that membership, or to enable the Government to become a member or party`) AND `the Minister consulted the Authority or the telecommunication licensee`

-- src:5544 | (3) Any direction given under subsection (1) or (2) may include —
-- src:5546 | (a) provisions for the prohibition or regulation of such use of
-- src:5547 | telecommunications in all cases or of such cases as may be
-- src:5548 | considered necessary;
-- src:5550 | (b) provisions for the taking of, the control of or the usage for
-- src:5551 | official purposes of, all or any such telecommunication
-- src:5552 | system and equipment; and
-- src:5554 | (c) provisions for the stopping, delaying and censoring of
-- src:5555 | messages and the carrying out of any other purposes which
-- src:5556 | the Minister thinks necessary.
@ref s 77(3) (src:5544-5556)
GIVEN provision IS A STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 77(3): a direction under subsection (1) or (2) may include this provision` MEANS
    elem provision (LIST "the prohibition or regulation of such use of telecommunications in all cases or of such cases as may be considered necessary"
                       , "the taking of, the control of or the usage for official purposes of, all or any such telecommunication system and equipment"
                       , "the stopping, delaying and censoring of messages and the carrying out of any other purposes which the Minister thinks necessary")

-- src:5558 | (4) Any direction given under subsection (3) does not apply to the
-- src:5559 | use of any telecommunications for the purpose of making or
-- src:5560 | answering signals of distress.
@ref s 77(4) (src:5558-5560)
GIVEN `the use is for the purpose of making or answering signals of distress` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 77(4): the direction applies to the use of telecommunications` MEANS
    NOT `the use is for the purpose of making or answering signals of distress`

-- src:5562 | (5) The Authority and any telecommunication licensee (as the case
-- src:5563 | may be) must give effect to any direction given to it under
-- src:5565 | Informal Consolidation – version in force from 2/10/2026
-- src:5566 | 113 Telecommunications Act 1999 2020 Ed.
-- src:5568 | subsection (1) or (2) despite any other duty imposed on the Authority
-- src:5569 | or the licensee by or under this Act.
@ref s 77(5) (src:5562-5569)
GIVEN `a direction was given under subsection (1) or (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 77(5): the Authority or telecommunication licensee must give effect to the direction despite any other duty under the Act` MEANS
    `a direction was given under subsection (1) or (2)`

-- src:5573 | (6) Any telecommunication licensee who contravenes
-- src:5574 | subsection (5) shall be guilty of an offence and shall be liable on
-- src:5575 | conviction —
-- src:5577 | (a) to a fine not exceeding the higher of the following
-- src:5578 | amounts:
-- src:5580 | (i) 10% of the annual turnover of that part of its business
-- src:5581 | in respect of which it is granted the licence, as
-- src:5582 | ascertained from its latest audited accounts; or
-- src:5584 | (ii) $1 million; and
-- src:5586 | (b) in the case of a continuing offence, to a further fine not
-- src:5587 | exceeding $100,000 for every day or part of a day during
-- src:5588 | which the offence continues after conviction.
@ref s 77(6) (src:5573-5588)
GIVEN `the telecommunication licensee contravenes subsection (5)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `annual turnover in dollars of that part of its business in respect of which it is granted the licence, from the latest audited accounts` IS A NUMBER
      `the offence is a continuing offence after conviction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 77(6): the most the fine may be on conviction, in dollars, for the offence` MEANS
    BRANCH IF NOT `the telecommunication licensee contravenes subsection (5)` THEN NOTHING
           IF (`annual turnover in dollars of that part of its business in respect of which it is granted the licence, from the latest audited accounts` TIMES 0.1) GREATER THAN 1000000 THEN JUST (`annual turnover in dollars of that part of its business in respect of which it is granted the licence, from the latest audited accounts` TIMES 0.1)
           OTHERWISE JUST 1000000

GIVEN `the telecommunication licensee contravenes subsection (5)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the offence continues after conviction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 77(6)(b): the most the further fine may be for every day or part of a day, in dollars` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `the telecommunication licensee contravenes subsection (5)` AND `the offence continues after conviction` THEN JUST 100000
           OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:5592 | (7) The Authority and any telecommunication licensee must not
-- src:5593 | disclose any direction given to it under subsection (1) or (2) if the
-- src:5594 | Minister notifies the Authority or telecommunication licensee (as the
-- src:5595 | case may be) that the Minister is of the opinion that the disclosure of
-- src:5596 | the directions is against the public interest.
@ref s 77(7) (src:5592-5596)
GIVEN `the Minister notifies that the Minister is of the opinion that disclosure of the direction is against the public interest` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 77(7): the Authority or telecommunication licensee may disclose the direction` MEANS
    NOT `the Minister notifies that the Minister is of the opinion that disclosure of the direction is against the public interest`

-- src:5600 | (8) The Minister may —
-- src:5602 | (a) pay compensation for any damage caused to a
-- src:5603 | telecommunication licensee by reason of its compliance
-- src:5604 | with the directions of the Minister under subsection (3)(b);
-- src:5605 | or
-- src:5607 | (b) make grants to telecommunication licensees for defraying
-- src:5608 | or contributing towards any losses which they may sustain
-- src:5609 | by reason of their compliance with the directions of the
-- src:5610 | Minister under any other provision of this section.
@ref s 77(8) (src:5600-5610)
GIVEN `the damage was caused to a telecommunication licensee by reason of its compliance with a direction of the Minister under subsection (3)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the loss was sustained by reason of compliance with a direction of the Minister under any other provision of this section` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 77(8): the Minister may pay compensation or make a grant` MEANS
    `the damage was caused to a telecommunication licensee by reason of its compliance with a direction of the Minister under subsection (3)(b)` OR `the loss was sustained by reason of compliance with a direction of the Minister under any other provision of this section`

-- src:5614 | (9) Any sums required by the Minister for paying compensation or
-- src:5615 | making grants under subsection (8) must be paid out of the
-- src:5616 | Consolidated Fund.
@ref s 77(9) (src:5614-5616)
GIVEN `the sum is required by the Minister for paying compensation or making grants under subsection (8)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 77(9): the sum must be paid out of the Consolidated Fund` MEANS
    `the sum is required by the Minister for paying compensation or making grants under subsection (8)`

-- src:5621 | (10) If any doubt arises as to the existence of a public emergency or
-- src:5622 | as to whether any act done under this section was in the public interest
-- src:5623 | or in the interests of public security, national defence or relations with
-- src:5624 | the government of another country, a certificate signed by the
-- src:5625 | Minister is conclusive evidence of the matters stated in the certificate.
@ref s 77(10) (src:5621-5625)
GIVEN `a doubt arises as to the existence of a public emergency or as to whether an act done under this section was in the public interest or in the interests of public security, national defence or relations with the government of another country` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a certificate signed by the Minister states the matter` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 77(10): the certificate is conclusive evidence of the matters stated in it` MEANS
    `a doubt arises as to the existence of a public emergency or as to whether an act done under this section was in the public interest or in the interests of public security, national defence or relations with the government of another country` AND `a certificate signed by the Minister states the matter`

-- src:5627 | (11) This section does not authorise the Minister to give any
-- src:5628 | directions when an activation order (within the meaning of the Public
-- src:5629 | Order and Safety (Special Powers) Act 2018) is in force, and for any
-- src:5630 | of the purposes for which a direction under section 32 of that Act is or
-- src:5631 | may be given.
@ref s 77(11) (src:5627-5631)
GIVEN `an activation order within the meaning of the Public Order and Safety (Special Powers) Act 2018 is in force` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the direction is for a purpose for which a direction under section 32 of that Act is or may be given` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 77(11): the Minister is authorised by this section to give the direction` MEANS
    NOT (`an activation order within the meaning of the Public Order and Safety (Special Powers) Act 2018 is in force` AND `the direction is for a purpose for which a direction under section 32 of that Act is or may be given`)
